L0228: Evidence application has the wrong arguments

Only evidence with a function-like logical conclusion, such as implication or universal evidence through its supported interface, can be applied. A proof of an unrelated proposition does not accept arbitrary arguments. Check the proposition and the required specialization operation.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/evidence_applied_to_nothing.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// Evidence of an equation takes no argument.
#[terminates] #[no_panic] #[no_io] fn first(h: @(1 == 1), n: u8) -> @(1 == 1) {
    h(n)
}
```

Language, as built: [1.7:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.7:1).
